WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.180
Hey guys, Pete here.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.270
This will be my Game of Thrones Season 8 episode
6 trailer breakdown.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:38.150
I wasn't expecting them to give away much
in the trailer, and unfortunately I was right.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:43.580
Still, we have some things to talk about in
this, and it is the final trailer for the

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.570
last episode of Game of Thrones ever.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.210
So, it's not like I was going to take the
day off after doing this for years.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.850
The first thing that stood out to me is that
whole trailer appears to be tied together

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.530
and related to a short period of time.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.980
Since we know episode 6 is another 80 minute
long episode this means that we're only looking

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:07.010
at a part of the series finale that we imagined
was inevitable anyway the time after the fighting

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:10.390
ends and Daenerys looks at what her victory
cost.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:15.880
I wondered as I looked at the last scene if
she's spoken to any of the people we see in

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:16.890
this trailer.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:21.560
I thought Arya returning was the most surprising
thing, and we'll talk about that after we

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.110
get through the images.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:27.640
Let's break it down scene by scene, all 9
of them, and then talk about where things

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.780
are headed.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.810
The episode 6 trailer opens with a shot of
Davos and Jon walking through the ruins of

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.050
King's Landing.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:39.780
We see fire burning inside a window behind
them, and a body on the ground in the front

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.979
of the frame.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:44.940
What stands out here is that there is a skeleton
on the left of the shot that looks like a

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.480
child to me.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.030
It's pretty gruesome.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:52.729
Even though we saw all that stuff go down
in episode 5 it's still pretty gruesome to

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:57.330
see the way that this small skeleton looks
framing that window there.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:01.729
There isn't any voiceover in this trailer
so we're left to wonder what these two characters

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:05.400
might be thinking as they walk through the
destruction.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:11.060
The next shot shows Tyrion walking alone doing
the same thing Jon and Davos probably doing.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.580
Taking in the reality of the destruction.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.110
We see blood smeared on the walls of the city
and fires still burning on the streets.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:22.020
We have to imagine that Tyrion is in a tough
position here after seeing how his plan to

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:25.520
stop the destruction himself didn't exactly
work out.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:31.080
We had the ominous warning from Daenerys that
the next time Tyrion failed her would be the

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.099
last time.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:37.129
And, I have to imagine this is going through
his head as he's walking towards the center

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:39.159
of town.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:41.140
After that we see what's left of the Red Keep.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:45.770
This doesn't reveal much since we witnessed
Daenerys attacking it in episode 5.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:50.900
Since it follows the shot of Tyrion this could
be from his perspective, and he would have

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.209
to be thinking about Cersei and Jaime.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:57.409
At this point he might still think its possible
that Jaime was able to reach Cersei and get

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:59.310
her out of King's Landing in time.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:03.550
I doubt by this time that Tyrion knows what
happened to them.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.200
Arya arrives next.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.819
We see the remaining Dothraki in front of
her, and she's probably going where we see

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:10.819
her next.

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:14.790
If you're keeping track Tyrion and Arya are
the only two characters that we see more than

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:19.700
once in this trailer and they are both moving
through the city alone.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:24.439
The next shot is of Arya again, and she's
standing behind the Unsullied.

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:28.459
Knowing what she lived through in episode
5 we can have a pretty good guess what's going

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:29.590
through her mind here.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:34.010
She is probably looking at Daenerys here,
and she looks absolutely vengeful as she is

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:37.870
processing the emotions that are running through
her.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.389
Then we see what's left of the Unsullied standing
looks like what's left of King's Landing.

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:45.890
They've followed their Queen a long way to
get to this place, and they should be coming

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.819
out of the battle in pretty good shape.

00:03:47.819 --> 00:03:51.930
All things considered it was a one-sided battle
so they shouldn't have taken too many casualties

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.719
during that.

00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:56.920
In the second shot we see of Tyrion he looks
deeply troubled.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.109
We get a good idea of how the ashes are covering
everything in this shot.

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:04.040
This reminds us of a couple things from past
seasons.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:08.989
In season 2 episode 8 Tyrion and Cersei are
talking about Joffrey fighting in the battle

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:10.099
of Blackwater.

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:15.120
Cersei tells Tyrion that she has his whore
as a hostage to make sure nothing happens

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.220
to Joffrey in that battle.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.940
After she presents Ros to him he tells her,
"I will hurt you for this.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.120
I don't know how yet, but give me time.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.250
A day will come when you think yourself safe
and happy and suddenly your joy will turn

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:29.750
to ashes in your mouth.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.850
And, you'll know the debt is paid."

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:36.990
So, even though in the end he tried to save
her and her unborn child he ended up paying

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.830
off what he told her in season 2.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:44.970
In season 7 we heard of ashes again when Tyrion
tells Daenerys, "Conquering Westeros would

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.180
be easy for you, but you're not here to be
Queen of the Ashes."

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.770
Daenerys itself echoes that later on when
she's talking to her allies about attacking

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:58.390
King's Landing by saying, "I'm not here to
be the Queen of Ashes."

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:02.350
This of course leads into one of Lady Ollena
giving one of her famous speeches.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.620
Saying, "He's a clever man, your hand.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.500
I've known many clever men.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.380
I've outlived them all, you know why?

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:09.560
I ignored them.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.790
The Lords of Westeros are sheep.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.790
Are you a sheep?

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.100
No, you're a dragon.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.150
Be a dragon."

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:20.110
In retrospect I'm not sure this is what the
Queen of Thorns had in mind, but there definitely

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:24.330
was some dragon going on in King's Landing
in episode 5.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:29.530
There is a quick look at the Dothraki cheering,
raising their weapons in the air.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:31.070
They look victorious.

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:32.910
They look happy with their victory.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:37.920
Then we see the closing shot of the trailer
as Daenerys walks out to address the assembled

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.920
soldiers.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:44.030
It's pretty clear that King's Landing is destroyed
here, and her troops at least seem to be satisfied

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.790
with what went down.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:52.500
As we saw in episode 5 she decided to be a
dragon, and so the Queen of Ashes it is.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:57.870
It's a very powerful image this last image,
and it really drives home the uncertainty

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.180
of how everything is going to go past this
scene.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:05.720
It's also clear that the other main characters
who followed Dany to this point are conflicted

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.470
about what just happened, and that's about
as far as they're going to go, and that's

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:13.340
about it for what they're going to give away
to us in this trailer.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:17.870
So, we have some scenes that look like they
take place directly after the battle.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:22.360
We can't tell how much time has passed, I
mean there are fires still burning out at

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:26.900
this point, but it's hard to imagine that
too much of the story will unfold before this

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.120
scene we have of Daenerys looking out over
the troops.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.030
Jon and Davos will most likely be reckoning
with what they just went through and thinking

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.530
about how to proceed.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:39.620
Beyond that we can only speculate on where
the rest of the episode might go.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.690
I'll wait until later this week to see if
they release any other pictures before I get

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:44.930
into all of that.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:47.340
The ashes in the trailer do make a good impression.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:52.470
Beyond the callbacks I mentioned above it
reminds me of the long running debate about

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.830
the visions from earlier seasons.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:59.410
In Daenerys' House of the Undying vision,
and later in Bran's weirwood vision we saw

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.260
the destroyed throne room.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:07.210
Ever since then people have debated over whether
it was ash or snow falling from the sky, and

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:09.270
I guess now we do know.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:13.660
Makes you wonder what the throne room will
actually look like we see Dany entering it

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.160
in episode 6.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.740
I mentioned being surprised about Arya's return.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:23.340
At the end of episode 5 I thought we might
be witnessing her riding away for good after

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.310
her conversation with the Hound.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:29.640
The fact that she returned makes you wonder
what part she'll play in the aftermath.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:34.090
Obviously we followed her harrowing journey
through the destruction so we know what she

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.090
saw.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:38.340
But, we also saw her change her mind about
killing Cersei.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:42.190
My guess is that a bunch of fans now will
jump on the idea that she's going to kill

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.870
Daenerys, and that would make some sense.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:49.200
There's the whole "green eyes" thing that
people keep bringing up in my comments [laughing].

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:54.961
But, I do wonder since it seems odd to have
her change her course in episode 5 only to

00:07:54.961 --> 00:07:57.920
re-up on being a killer in episode 6.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.550
I'm really not sure.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:04.460
Let me know what you guys think as far as
what part she'll play in the comments of this

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.460
video.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:09.430
If she's there as things are going down then
I have to expect she's going to play a part

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:10.840
in whatever comes next.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:16.310
So, being a main character, being involved,
it seems pretty important.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:20.670
In this trailer we don't see anyone from the
story who wasn't in King's Landing for the

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:21.720
battle.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:26.140
Episode 6 being the final episode of the entire
series means that we're definitely going to

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:30.920
be travelling north to Winterfell, or the
players that are there will be coming to King's

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.050
Landing.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:37.360
Daenerys framing her betrayal as Jon betraying
her by telling Sansa was one of the things

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.630
that really stood out to me in the last episode.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:44.620
While it seemed like there was a pretty good
chance Varys wouldn't make it out of the episode

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:50.750
alive, I was definitely surprised when Dany
shifted the blame for the betrayal from him

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.480
to Jon and Sansa.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:56.839
She gave Jon a chance to come back to her
and in that process called out Sansa for what

00:08:56.839 --> 00:08:57.880
she'd done.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:03.139
So, there's absolutely a conflict brewing
between these two characters.

00:09:03.139 --> 00:09:08.899
Besides Dany, Tyrion is certainly the character
in the toughest spot in the episode 6 trailer.

00:09:08.899 --> 00:09:13.370
As viewers we can understand what he did by
freeing Jaime, but based on the way things

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.079
played out we know that it's going to come
back up.

00:09:16.079 --> 00:09:20.710
I think it would be foolish to try to suppose
what's actually going through the Queen's

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:21.850
mind at this point.

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:27.329
I went over the path that she traveled to
reach this destination in my video yesterday,

00:09:27.329 --> 00:09:31.499
but we're in the dark as far depth she's sunk
to at this time.

00:09:31.499 --> 00:09:33.769
This makes Tyrion's outcome uncertain.

00:09:33.769 --> 00:09:37.310
On the one hand he could explain away the
fact that he freed Jaime based on wanting

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:42.680
to get Cersei to surrender, and he is essentially
the only adviser she has left.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:47.610
On the other hand what are the chances that
Daenerys will be keen to see this in any other

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:50.470
way than a betrayal?

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.970
That's about all there is to say about this
trailer.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:57.279
We still have 80 minutes of story left to
tell so there's a lot that can happen.

00:09:57.279 --> 00:10:00.790
Let me know in the comments what you guys
think about how they're going to wrap things

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:01.790
up.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:05.889
Please like the video if you enjoyed it, please
subscribe to my channel if you haven't already.

00:10:05.889 --> 00:10:11.379
We're getting ready to watch the final episode
of the series and I look forward to doing

00:10:11.379 --> 00:10:12.379
that with you.

00:10:12.379 --> 00:10:14.609
Thanks for watching, I will talk to you soon.

